
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<interface>
  <requires lib="gtk" version="4.0"/>

  
<!-- Text buffer that contains hard-coded text -->
  <object class="GtkTextBuffer" id="buffer">
    <property name="text">GTK4 application using the PTX205R and the RUL SDK v1.3.0 reference implementation for the Raspberry Pi and SPI.

Polls for RF-technologies A, B, F, V.

Polling tab: the discovery settings - idle time, low power card detection (LPCD), digital dynamic power control (DDPC) and, per RF-technology, enable, poll frequency, max. number of devices and the Type-F bit rate (212 or 424 kbit/s). Settings are used the next time discovery is started and are not stored.

Discovery tab: all cards in the field (up to 5 per RF-technology, 20 in total per discovery cycle) are displayed in a table, with RF-technology, protocol, nominal bit rate, ID, the number of detections and technology-specific details. Detected cards stay in the list until discovery is restarted (STOP and START, or RESET). Discovery is started and stopped with START/STOP, RESET clears the list and restarts discovery.

NDEF tab: only one single card in the field is supported. READ starts discovery and reads the NDEF message of activated cards, STOP stops it and CLEAR clears the output. If a card is activated, a one-line card summary (RF-technology, protocol, ID) is displayed, followed by the NDEF records of the card in decoded form (URI, Text, Smart Poster, MIME, absolute URI, external types) and the raw bytes of the NDEF message. NDEF messages can also be composed from standard record types (URI, Text, Smart Poster, Phone, Email, SMS, Geo location, vCard, MIME, Wi-Fi, Android app) and written to a card with WRITE. Writing waits for a card for max. 10 polling cycles, then stops discovery.

HCE tab: host card emulation - the PTX205R emulates an NFC-A Type 4 Tag carrying an NDEF message, composed with the same editor as on the NDEF tab (default: URI https://www.renesas.com/en/products/ptx205r). The emulation is started and stopped with START/STOP. The tag is writable: an NDEF message written by a reader is displayed, together with an emulation log. Every START resets the tag to the message of the editor.

Q-Measurement tab: measures the Q factor of the antenna. The PTX sweeps through a frequency range centered on 13.56 MHz (settings: frequency span, frequency step and ADC averaging) and the RF amplitude is measured at every frequency and shown in a graph while the sweep is running. START/STOP starts and ends the sweep. When the sweep is complete, the resonance frequency, the -3 dB corner frequencies, the bandwidth and the Q factor are calculated and displayed. EXPORT CSV saves the last sweep. Settings are not stored.

THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

This application dynamically links against GTK4, GLib and Gio (LGPL v2.1 or later) and the libraries they depend on (Pango, Cairo, HarfBuzz, gdk-pixbuf and others, mostly LGPL, MIT/X11 or BSD; liblzo2 and libjbig0 are GPL v2 or later). They are used unmodified and can be replaced by newer versions. Source code: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gtk, https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/glib and https://sources.debian.org. The license texts are in the files COPYING and COPYING.LESSER and, for every library of the AppImage, in usr/share/doc/&lt;package&gt;/copyright. See also DEPENDENCIES.md and license.txt.

Logging: zf_log 0.4.0, Copyright 2017 wonder-mice, MIT License. Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy of this software and associated documentation files (the "Software"), to deal in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions: The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all copies or substantial portions of the Software. THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.

PTX205R firmware / uCode image: Renesas Open License v1.0, Copyright (c) 2020 - 2026, Renesas Electronics Corporation and/or its affiliates. The firmware may only be used with a Renesas integrated circuit and must not be reverse engineered, decompiled, modified or disassembled. The license text is in the file Renesas_Open_License_v1.txt.

